# Live SEO metadata must match ditto

`<title>`, meta description, Open Graph (`og:title`, `og:description`, images), and Twitter card tags on stage **must match live** (`azmortgagebrothers.com`) character-for-character for the same route.

## Source of truth

- Registry: `lib/seo-metadata.json` (route pathname → live meta)
- Helper: `lib/seo.ts` → `getSeoMetadata(pathname)`
- Refresh from live: `node scripts/refresh-live-seo-meta.mjs`

## Brand names in meta are NOT exempt

The body-copy brand rule (`brand-name-not-a-mismatch.mdc`) does **not** apply to SEO metadata.

If live uses “Arizona Mortgage Brothers”, “AZ Mortgage Brothers”, or “Arizona Home Loans | The Mortgage Brothers” in title/description/OG/Twitter, stage must use that **exact** string. Do **not** rewrite meta brand tokens to “Mortgage Brothers LLC”.

```text
// ✅ REQUIRED (live → stage meta)
Live title:  Arizona Mortgage Brothers | Phoenix Home Loan Broker
Stage title: Arizona Mortgage Brothers | Phoenix Home Loan Broker

// ❌ NEVER (brand rewrite in meta)
Stage title: Mortgage Brothers LLC | Phoenix Home Loan Broker
```

## Non-negotiable

- When adding or editing a page, set `export const metadata = getSeoMetadata("/your-slug/")` from the registry — do not invent alternate titles/descriptions.
- If live meta is missing for a new route, scrape live first and add the entry to `lib/seo-metadata.json` before shipping.
- `og:site_name` stays the live value: `Arizona Home Loans | The Mortgage Brothers` (`OG_SITE_NAME` in `lib/seo.ts`).
- Body/UI brand naming may still follow stage branding; **meta tags do not**.
